  "judge": {
    "dimensions": [
      {
        "name": "Required check",
        "score": 4,
        "rationale": "No concurrency group was added, but the trigger sets are not disjoint: `labeled` still triggers the workflow and a job-level `if` only skips `test`. That skipped run posts a new `test` check on the same head SHA, which GitHub treats as passing, so labeling a PR can mask an earlier failing `test` run instead of keeping the triggers separate (for example, a separate workflow file for label events)."
      },
      {
        "name": "Behavior",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "Adding the `e2e` label still starts the end-to-end suite, an unrelated label on an `e2e` PR no longer re-runs it, and `test` still runs on opened, synchronize and reopened, although the unchanged `on:` block isn't shown in the diff."
      },
      {
        "name": "Restraint",
        "score": 10,
        "rationale": "Only `.github/workflows/ci.yml` was changed; the ruleset and the rest of the repository were left alone, and the agent said plainly that the change is untested and the live ruleset unchecked."
      }
    ],
